From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iCosiSenpai <aod-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:29:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aod: restart from the in-game menu for settings read at start

The action bar shows Restart while a setting read only at start holds another value than it had when the game
started, and hides it again once every such setting is back. The status line follows the same rule instead of
staying on "restart" after the first change. Restart writes the settings, then ends the game with the exit code the
launcher names in AOD_RESTART_EXIT, so the launcher starts it again; without that variable there is no button.
Quit also writes a change made a moment ago before the game closes.

The menu preview stubs the two new platform calls; two scenarios check the button appears, disappears, starts the
restart with the setting written, and stays hidden without a launcher that restarts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
